<div class=mywhitetext>

<h3>Primary and Alternate Characters<o:p></o:p></h3>

<h4 style='margin-right:.5in;margin-left:.5in'>Primaries are Primary, alts are
secondary<o:p></o:p></h4>

<p style='margin-right:.5in;margin-left:.5in'>Each member of Bloodhorde is
required to specify their primary character. Your primary character is the
character that you spend the most time playing. You may specify only one primary
character. Primary characters get the full benefit of the guild. This includes
rewards, gifts, and first chance at raid loot. However, primary characters have
the one requirement that you must advance the character at least 1 level of
experience every 3 weeks until you reach level 50. After that, the requirement
is dropped. If you fail to do so, the character will be assigned to the Blood
Minion rank. Again, this is to encourage people to play their primary
characters as much as possible. <o:p></o:p></p>

<p style='margin-right:.5in;margin-left:.5in'>Blood Minions, or alternate
characters still have access to the guild treasury and library. However, alt
characters will not be allowed to advance beyond Blood Minion, which means they
will always be behind primary characters for loot on raids. <o:p></o:p></p>

<p style='margin-right:.5in;margin-left:.5in'>Bloodhorde will allow you to have
up to 3 alternate characters in Bloodhorde. However, your primary character
must be at least level 35 and obtain the rank of 'Horde Member' before we will
allow you to have any alternate characters in Bloodhorde. At level 40, we will
allow you to have 2, and at level 50, we will allow you to have 3 alternates. <o:p></o:p></p>

<p style='margin-right:.5in;margin-left:.5in'>Bloodhorde does not wish to tell
people how to play their account. However, one of our goals is to someday do
dragon and plane raids. We want to encourage people to play their primary characters
as much as possible so that we will all be lvl 50+ some day. We do not want a
guild full of lvl 30's. Alternate characters should be thought of as the
characters you play when you cannot get a group for your primary. <o:p></o:p></p>

<p style='margin-right:.5in;margin-left:.5in'>Note that your alternate characters
must also meet the standard <a
href="membership.htm">Bloodhorde
Membership</a> guidelines (evil, min lvl 24, etc.). <o:p></o:p></p>


